\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Definition}
\title{Sources over a commutative ring}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{For the \vocabk{ring paired coefficient}{fdip-00TJ}, let
#{\mathcal B(V)} be an independent copy of #{\mathcal A(V)}
with universal odd vector #{\eta} and covector #{\bar\eta}.
Work in #{\mathcal B(V)\widehat\otimes_k\mathcal A(V)}:
source and field generators anticommute, and source coefficients
are written first. Extend #{\mathcal I_V} by
#{\mathcal B(V)}-linearity. The \newvocab{ring source polynomial}
of any endomorphism #{K} is
##{\mathscr Z_K(\bar\eta,\eta)
 =\mathcal I_V\extexp
 \bigl(-\bar\psi(K\psi)+\bar\eta(\psi)+\bar\psi(\eta)\bigr).}
The finite exterior exponential is taken in the combined
source and field algebra. Every argument in this display is
quadratic; neither an inverse kernel nor a factorial inverse
is part of the definition.}
